{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for the full N2 design/source delivery at exact 7f49d9e4dbb96525a8f4ffa484d00078de4d3595, invitation 82191a0b, my promise e6b2bd24 and sole subject 12093e3c. The actor, agreement and race model is coherent, but the attention table and compatible-admission semantic context need two small corrections. Normal assigned prepare binds only to original design/source-note request 9c43c173 and promise 6f1481eb. It does not close the later exact W0 amendment or runtime implementation, or adopt the composable successor mechanisms.\n\nP2 — Notify parties whose pending responsibility is displaced or ended. The Transfer row at line172 and declaration at499 permit a performer to replace an existing pending transfer. At revision r, P offers to S1; at r+1, P offers to S2. The second act replaces both transfer and successor. Yet Transfer's attention row732 names only the successor after and the requester. S1 receives no notice that its offer is no longer current, unlike Agree730, Cancel731 and Report735, which explicitly notify the successor they clear.\n\nAdd the successor before to Transfer's recipients when replaced, alongside the successor after and requester, deduplicating the same member. Preserve the ability to renegotiate a transfer unless the owner deliberately chooses to refuse replacement; no new lifecycle restriction is required. Also include a distinct acceptor when Withdraw/Close/Supersede ends a reported item (737): Report735 told that acceptor to judge, but termination currently omits them, whereas Cancel731 includes them. Specify the cancellation/closure of their pending attention and preserve its historical subject. Notifications remain information, not a grant or proof of external delivery. Align the table, declared intents and compact fixtures; these two short before/after cases need no runtime probe or numerical test quota.\n\nP2 — State which evaluator context admits a compatible transition. The pinned definition includes steps version, evaluator profile, record, opening guards/effect and transition guards/effects at552–557. Compatibility at562–566 compares only the active kind's guard/effect bytes. Replay at582–587 expressly interprets the pinned steps version/profile. Admission does not state that same condition equally explicitly. A later document with a different evaluator context and identical guard/effect text can therefore pass the stated comparison without a clear rule about which meaning admission applies.\n\nSpecify that compatible admission evaluates the guards and effect under the thread's pinned steps version/profile and record definition. If the implementation cannot do that, refuse definition-mismatch. Alternatively require unchanged evaluator context as part of compatibility. Keep current role, roster, delegation and kind binding checks current, as already stated; they must not overwrite agreed terms or party/reference guards. Align the compatibility paragraph, replay and W0 acceptance case. This is a missing design condition, not an executed divergence: exact W0 semantics and differing profiles are unimplemented. Refusal is an acceptable outcome; this does not demand retention of an old Artroom engine or backward compatibility.\n\nSmaller clarification. The counter-offer description at185 restricts prospective performers, while the counter declaration at508 is a role-only comment with no party guard. It cannot change item state or accepted terms, so this is not an authority bypass. State whether anyone with the comment role may make an advisory counter-offer, or how the eligibility classification is enforced. Avoid claiming that a cosmetic comment enforces a stateful actor rule. W0 must also state the current versus pinned meaning of notification declarations and the retained evidence needed for external member/reference guards during replay; those are already owned exact-contract details, not delivered capabilities.\n\nArchitecture. Work item, personal commitment and leased hold are separate, and performer need not be holder. Filing needs no repository hold; decline leaves work open; cancellation returns it to open; report/rejection preserve the commitment; only the fixed acceptor's acceptance satisfies the item. Requester/admin closure is an attributed different outcome. A landing is report evidence rather than requester satisfaction. A fixed member remains a party across key recovery, while removal and irrecoverable authority have explicit closure options without invented acceptance.\n\nOffered and accepted terms are separate immutable act references. Amendment never changes accepted terms until the performer's explicit agreement. Each agreement and take-over becomes a new current commitment naming its predecessor; reports name that commitment. The two-agent example preserves both accepted terms and context, and transfers no responsibility until the successor acts. A required revision guard serializes effective transitions, while comments/counter-offers do not spuriously move it. Both cancellation/report and cancellation/acceptance orders are stated, including non-code completion, lease expiry and policy activation. A lost response requires replaying the exact prepared act; a later revision refusal cannot establish the earlier outcome.\n\nThe general record/guard/effect capability is a useful design direction. Party slots change only through passed effects; fixed slots are set only at filing. Signer/party guards supplement role checks, so admin role does not impersonate a requester or acceptor. Explicit relation guards prevent arbitrary acts, self-duplicates and wrong-definition duplicates; replacements can use a newer definition without silently migrating a promise. Finality refuses transitions, while retained comments and bounded cycle presentation preserve history. The chosen one-performer lifecycle is an application policy, not a platform cap on contributors.\n\nSecurity. Present authority and pinned historical meaning remain different inputs. A new role or policy does not reinterpret an accepted commitment. Refused and unrecorded binding-stale requests are distinguished from recorded state refusals and admitted comments with no cooperative effect. All reference/member guards are required in addition to format validation. Exact replay must derive the state change rather than trusting receipt effects. Future admission, read and verifier implementations need to agree on pinned semantics and complete evidence; source prose alone establishes none of those capabilities.\n\nPublication and cancellation limits are explicit. Before the existing landing reservation, item withdrawal still does not stop a separately judged lane landing; after reservation publication completes forward. Neither outcome says withdrawn work was accepted or that a published effect did not occur. Stopping publication through an item rule is not delivered by this note. Under the current successor commissioning, R3's exact publication/fencing decision must remain separately reviewed and adopted. Removing the predecessor does not delete an actual reserved or unknown external duty.\n\nThe cooperative option is honestly reduced. It distinguishes Room admission from application interpretation, pins its reading rule/source and stops at a history gap or unsupported meaning. Complete-prefix state is anchored to a stated log position/publication watermark and advances through bounded pages. Wrong actors and closed-work comments may be recorded there, but cannot be represented as platform enforcement. This optional practice cannot close N2's enforced lifecycle or replace the later W0–W7 route. It is also not a universal first-Jam gate.\n\nSimplification and breadth of value. Keep one authoritative item record, one revision and an attributable agreement chain, with a generic bounded primitive capability rather than an app-specific protocol shortcut. Show offered versus accepted terms, exact report/commitment and who owes the next act in ordinary product language. Show refusals and uncertainty directly; do not require a person to reconstruct state from an agent transcript. Complete attention includes the person losing an offer or judgment duty as well as the new recipient. Keep shared compact lifecycle invariants reusable at the reading-rule and actual admission boundaries, without per-field sweeps or a whole-platform gate for each screen.\n\nComplete scope. I read the original full N2 commissioning and the exact note's actor/state/transition/authority/attention/race tables, two worked examples, full handoff and twelve fixtures. Negotiated conditions, unheld filing, optional addressing/scope, decline, withdrawal before/after promise, performer cancellation, handover, reporting, rejection/acceptance, non-landing closure, supersession and retained links remain owed. W0 supplies the later exact types/forms/validation/definition/refusal/receipt/read contract; W4 policy, W5 verifier before producer, W6 admission, W7 declarations/client and W2/W3 public views/agent path deliver enforcement. W8 and the full N6 manual remain owed. Optional W1 is not a prerequisite and not delivery of the enforced route. Exact W0 needs its own review/adoption before separately commissioned runtime work.\n\nHugh's d4e07064 direction and the now current jointly reviewed/adopted017/018 planning inputs require complete successor retarget/removal. This predecessor Room/thread/steps-v2 design does not reinstate old-format/client/reader compatibility or preapprove detailed R1/R2/R3/R4 choices. Carry the useful lifecycle and agreement/attention/uncertainty outcomes into their independently adopted successor definitions and give every retained or removed component its actual task/disposition. All browser outcomes, split/contribution/join/qualified review, public-package outsider use, manual/replay/deployed acceptance and complete replacement scope remain intact. The schedule does not reduce them. Accepted promises and real effect duties need their own formal reconciliation; no category table or engine removal satisfies them.\n\nIndependent evidence. I read every byte of the exact note: 62,316 bytes/982 lines, SHA256 c242635923be9a023a124de807ab52137058d80e4c05fc876aa3688e442798bb, Git blob6dad18a7d8b449d8b5e64eb34f4cdc0a2ff5b5e3. Raw artifact payload head/path match, and its sole raw Rests-On is original promise6f1481eb. The registered isolated checkout is clean at the exact head. The full original request and invitation were read. Historical d691e6e9 source excerpts independently confirm RuleInput has no item state and declared member/act fields check format only. Existing policy has one named evaluator profile; the finding concerns the incomplete future compatibility rule, not a currently demonstrated alternate-profile attack. Historical source classifications remain historical, not present-day delivery claims.\n\nOne user-authorized parallel static audit assisted the attention and definition checks. I independently read the whole subject and verified the concrete before/after triggers. No source changes, tests, install, typecheck, build, repository-code execution, private diagnostic, live-provider effect, deployment or person contact occurred. The earlier rejected private diagnostic was not rerun, rewritten, extended or delegated; no native reviewer/task/model/backend replacement or restriction override was used.\n\nDisposition. Correct the attention and compatible-admission conditions in the design and successor handoff, retain the complete original commissioning, publish exact current revised evidence and return for ordinary independent review. This changes-requested design verdict authorizes no landing, exact W0 adoption or runtime implementation.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:12093e3c5994a85dedcaa5238faaf9d03fb2fdde","binding":"assigned","head":"7f49d9e4dbb96525a8f4ffa484d00078de4d3595","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1: